course: dictionary
lesson: 11956
title: Carsick: feeling sick on the road
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Carsick means feeling sick, dizzy or wanting to vomit when you travel in a car or bus. «Ravi felt carsick on the winding road to the hills.» Winding roads have lots of bends, so Ravi's tummy got upset.
explain: Read the words around a new word to work out its meaning. «Mum packed a bag, just in case Lily felt carsick on the bus.» A bag is for being sick in, so carsick must link to feeling ill on a journey. Check it: "just in case Lily felt sick or dizzy on the bus" makes sense.
explain: Some children get carsick on long or winding journeys. Your eyes and your inner ears, which sense balance and movement, can send your brain different messages, and that can make you feel ill. You can feel better by looking out of the front window at the far-off horizon, getting fresh air and taking breaks.
fact: Carsick means feeling sick, dizzy or wanting to vomit when travelling in a car or bus.
fact: Carsickness is the noun: «Carsickness spoiled the long drive for Ruby.»
fact: «Winding» roads, with lots of bends, often make people carsick.
fact: Your eyes and inner ears send your brain different messages, which can make you carsick.
fact: To feel better, look at the horizon, get fresh air, take breaks and avoid reading in the car.
exercise: What does carsick mean? | Feeling cold in a car with the windows open | Feeling tired after a long football match | *Feeling sick or dizzy when travelling in a car or bus
exercise: Which word in «Ravi felt carsick on the winding road» tells you the road had lots of bends? | felt | road | Ravi | *winding
exercise: Which tip could help someone who feels carsick? | Stare down at your phone | Read a comic with your head down all the way | *Look out of the front window at the far-off horizon | Shut every window tight and sit in silence
test: Carsickness is best described as which of these? | A bus driver who likes to drive fast | A car that has been sick on the seats | *The feeling of being carsick | A broken engine in an old car
test: What does «Mum packed a bag, just in case Lily felt carsick» suggest? | The bus was going to be late | Lily was going to the beach for a swim | Lily had lost her bag on the bus | *Lily might feel sick on the journey
exam: Which is the best meaning of carsick? | Driving very fast on a country road | Being a car mechanic who fixes engines | Sleeping peacefully in the back seat | *Feeling sick, dizzy or wanting to vomit on a car or bus journey
